    "result_text": "The build is green. The full test suite (the `AcceptanceTest` with its 3 checkpoints) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created (`POST /api/owners`).\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `OwnerAddress.java`: a `normalize(String)` that trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). `null` stays `null`; a whitespace-only value becomes `\"\"`. The transformation is idempotent, following the same pattern as the existing `OwnerTelephone`/`OwnerEmail` helpers.\n\n**Wiring changes:**\n\n1. **`ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 normalizes the address into the request body up front, *before* the required-field check. This means the stored/returned `address` is the normalized form, and the blank check now rejects an address that is blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"` \u2192 `\"\"` \u2192 400).\n\n2. **`EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 household duplicate detection now compares addresses via `OwnerAddress.normalize` (applied to both request and existing owners, so pre-existing/seed data is normalized on the fly), instead of the old lowercase+collapse form. Last-name comparison is unchanged.\n\n3. **`AssignOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 the shared `householdId` derivation and housemate matching now use the same normalized address form, keeping every household member consistent.\n\nThis satisfies the three behaviors the spec called out: normalized whitespace/case (`\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`), abbreviation expansion (`\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`), and rejecting an address blank after normalization \u2014 while routing every address comparison through the normalized form.",
